{
  "$schema": "https://yamcs.org/schema/stack.schema.json",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_ENABLE_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": []
    },
    {
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/DEVICE_ENABLED",
          "operator": "eq",
          "value": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Sun point (mode 2, SUNSAFE).",
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_SET_MODE_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "MODE",
          "value": "SUNSAFE"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/SUN_X",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "0.98"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/SUN_Y",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/SUN_Y",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/SUN_Z",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/SUN_Z",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 120000
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Nadir point (mode 3): no dedicated ground-visible check existed for this mode before -- only unit tests. Shares adcs_point_vector_controller() with target-track, so the same qn scalar-order fix applies here too.",
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_SET_MODE_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "MODE",
          "value": "NADIR"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Rates near zero proves it stopped moving; POINT_VEC_BODY_X/Y/Z near (1,0,0) proves it stopped moving AT the actual nadir goal, not just somewhere -- POINT_VEC_BODY is adcs_point_vector_controller()'s normalized body-frame input vector (nadir_body here), the same kind of direct pointing-accuracy check SUN_X/Y/Z already gives SUNSAFE above. Longer timeout than the SUNSAFE step's own budget isn't needed here, but 90s (vs. the previous 30s) gives real settle margin against a wilder-than-nominal initial tumble. MODE==3 is bundled in specifically so this can't pass on a stale pre-switch HK sample still carrying SUNSAFE's already-converged values -- the verify tool (yamcs_commander.py's _run_verify_step) checks whatever the latest sample happens to be the instant it's called, with no guaranteed minimum wait for a fresh one, so without this a same-shaped check right after a mode switch can spuriously pass on leftover telemetry from before the switch took effect.",
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/MODE",
          "operator": "eq",
          "value": "3"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_X",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_X",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Y",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Y",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Z",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Z",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_X",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "0.98"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Y",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Y",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Z",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Z",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 90000
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Target zenith (anti-nadir) via the new SET_TARGET_VECTOR_CC (issue follow-up), standing in for 'the Moon' pending real ephemeris wiring (42 tracks World[LUNA] internally, but it is not yet piped through simulith's IPC protocol to ADCS -- see conversation notes). Deliberately the negation of the nadir direction (nadir_inertial[i] = -pos_n[i] in adcs_sim.c) at nominal-baseline's initial orbital position, rather than an arbitrary vector, so this step forces a real ~180-degree slew away from the just-verified NADIR pointing instead of a coincidental near-no-op. Also un-normalized (scaled x2 from the unit direction) to keep exercising the device's on-receipt normalization.",
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_SET_TARGET_VECTOR_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "TARGET_X",
          "value": "-1.8794"
        },
        {
          "name": "TARGET_Y",
          "value": "-0.4209"
        },
        {
          "name": "TARGET_Z",
          "value": "0.5391"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "name": "/ADCS/ADCS_SET_MODE_CC",
      "extraOptions": [],
      "arguments": [
        {
          "name": "MODE",
          "value": "TARGET"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Same pointing-accuracy upgrade as the NADIR step above: rates near zero plus POINT_VEC_BODY_X/Y/Z near (1,0,0) proves target-track actually converged onto the commanded zenith vector, not just that it stopped moving somewhere. 90s timeout (vs. the previous 30s) for settle margin against a wilder-than-nominal initial tumble. MODE==4 is bundled in for the same reason as NADIR's step above -- this is the antipodal target to NADIR's, so without it, a stale pre-switch sample still showing NADIR's own just-converged (1,0,0) pointing would spuriously satisfy this identically-shaped check before target-track has actually done anything (confirmed live: this exact scenario passed step 8 in 0.028s with ANGRATE/POINT_VEC_BODY values bit-identical to NADIR's step, before this fix).",
      "type": "verify",
      "condition": [
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/MODE",
          "operator": "eq",
          "value": "4"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_X",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_X",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Y",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Y",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Z",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/ANGRATE_Z",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_X",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "0.98"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Y",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Y",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Z",
          "operator": "lt",
          "value": "0.02"
        },
        {
          "parameter": "/ADCS/POINT_VEC_BODY_Z",
          "operator": "gt",
          "value": "-0.02"
        }
      ],
      "timeout": 90000
    }
  ],
  "advancement": {
    "acknowledgment": "Acknowledge_Sent",
    "wait": 1000
  }
}
